              "text": "**\"Still in Love with You\"** is a track by the legendary country music duo **Brooks & Dunn**, released on their multi-platinum debut studio album, ***Brand New Man* (1991)**. \n\nHere is a breakdown of the key details, lyrics, and interesting facts about the song:\n\n### 1. Key Facts\n* **Songwriters:** Kix Brooks, Ronnie Dunn, and Don Cook.\n* **Lead Vocals:** Unlike many of the duo's massive radio hits (which were sung by Ronnie Dunn), **Kix Brooks** sings the lead vocals on this particular track. \n* **Release:** While it wasn't pushed as a major radio single, it was included as the B-side to their second consecutive #1 hit single, \"My Next Broken Heart,\" in September 1991.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Lyrics Snippet\nThe song is a melancholy, bittersweet country ballad about having to say goodbye to a lover while still being completely in love with them. \n\n**Verse 1:**\n> *My taxicab is waiting*\n> *Wish I could hold you one last time*\n> *After all we've had together*\n> *There's gotta be a better way*\n> *Of telling you goodbye...*\n\n**Chorus:**\n> *If I had a horse, I'd ride off in the sunset*\n> *If I had wings, I'd fly off in the sky so blue*\n> *If I had the time, I'd spend my whole life dreaming*\n> *But I'd wake up, still in love with you.*\n\n**Verse 2:**\n> *Be in Baton Rouge by morning*\n> *Hope you're missing me by then*\n> *I'd like to be the kind of memory*\n> *That makes you want to take me back*\n> *In your arms again...*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Where to Listen\nBecause it is part of their iconic debut album *Brand New Man*, you can easily stream it on:\n* **YouTube / YouTube Music** (Search: *\"Brooks and Dunn - Still in Love with You\"*)\n* **Spotify, Apple Music, and Amazon Music** under the *Brand New Man* album.",
